{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — templates/page.membership.liquid
  ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Alternate page template. In the admin: Pages → HIVOLT Circuit — Membership →
  Template suffix → "membership". Renders inside layout/theme.liquid, which
  supplies <main>.

  Styles live in site/theme/pages.css. build-theme.py concatenates that into
  the single assets/hivolt.css that layout/theme.liquid already links, after
  theme-hivolt.css — so there is no second stylesheet to add.

  Uses Shopify's native customer form — form 'customer'. Field names matter:

      contact[email]       → the address, validated by Shopify
      contact[first_name]  → optional, used only to address the email
      contact[tags]        → applied to the created customer record; "newsletter"
                             is the tag Shopify's own marketing surfaces read

  form.posted_successfully? is only true on the redirect after a successful
  submit, so the confirmation renders above a fresh, empty form. form.errors is
  rendered as a real list with role="alert" rather than a colour change, because
  a colour change is invisible to a screen reader.

  The page states no member discount, no points balance and no tier. The store
  operates none of those, and a benefit that does not exist is the one thing a
  signup page must not print.
{%- endcomment -%}

<nav class="crumb wrap" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
    <li aria-current="page">{{ page.title | default: 'Membership' | escape }}</li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<section class="hero hero--doc wrap">
  <p class="mono hero__eyebrow">The Circuit</p>
  <h1 class="hero__h">Told first.<br>Nothing<br><em>else sent.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero__sub">
    Free to join. One email when a drop is coming, one when it's live. No weekly
    newsletter, because there isn't one.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pg wrap">
  <div class="cf__grid">

    <div>
      {%- form 'customer', id: 'circuit-signup' -%}

      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        <div class="cf__ok" tabindex="-1" role="status">
          <p class="mono cf__ok-h">You're on the list</p>
          <p class="cf__ok-b">
            Nothing else to do. The next message you get from us will be a drop
            going live — every email carries an unsubscribe link.
          </p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}


        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div class="cf__err" tabindex="-1" role="alert">
            <p class="mono cf__err-h">That didn't go through</p>
            <ul class="cf__err-l">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>
                  {%- if field == 'form' -%}
                    {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] }} — {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="cf">
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter, circuit">

          <div class="cf__f">
            <label class="cf__l" for="circuit-name">First name</label>
            <input class="cf__in" type="text" id="circuit-name"
                   name="contact[first_name]" autocomplete="given-name"
                   value="{{ form.first_name }}">
            <p class="cf__h">Optional. Only used to address the email.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="cf__f">
            <label class="cf__l" for="circuit-email">
              Email<span class="cf__req" aria-hidden="true">required</span>
            </label>
            <input class="cf__in" type="email" id="circuit-email"
                   name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" required
                   value="{{ form.email }}"
                   placeholder="you@example.com">
          </div>

          <button class="btn cf__go" type="submit">Join the Circuit</button>

          <p class="cf__note">
            Unsubscribe from any email. The address is used for drop notices and
            nothing else — it is not sold, and it is not passed to an advertiser.
          </p>
        </div>

      {%- endform -%}
    </div>

    <aside class="pg__aside">
      <p class="mono pg__aside-h">What you get</p>
      <div class="rte rte--tight">
        {%- if page.content != blank -%}
          {{ page.content }}
        {%- else -%}
          <ul>
            <li>Notice before a drop goes live.</li>
            <li>First access while a limited run lasts.</li>
            <li>Nothing between drops.</li>
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <p class="mono pg__aside-h pg__aside-h--gap">What it isn't</p>
      <div class="rte rte--tight">
        <p>
          There is no members' discount, no points balance and no tier to climb.
          The Circuit is a notification list. Saying otherwise would be the
          easiest thing on this page to write and the first thing to be untrue.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mono pg__aside-h pg__aside-h--gap">Already have an account?</p>
      <div class="rte rte--tight">
        <p>
          An account and the Circuit are separate. <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}">Your
          account</a> holds orders and addresses; this list holds nothing but an
          email address.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="pg__qw wrap">
  <div class="pg__q">
    <p class="pg__q-t">
      <span class="mono">Want to see what's live first?</span>
      The current drop is on the calendar, with every style's fibre composition
      and fabric weight published against it.
    </p>
    {%- assign drops_page = pages['drops'] -%}
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="{{ drops_page.url | default: '/pages/drops' }}">Drop calendar</a>
  </div>
</section>
